license-url: "https://github.com/ai-sci-computing/covmg/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-20"
keywords:
  - connection Laplacian
  - magnetic Laplacian
  - Bochner Laplacian
  - geometric multigrid
  - gauge covariance
  - eigenvalue problem
  - LOBPCG
  - lattice gauge theory
  - vortex filament extraction
  - fluid simulation
abstract: >-
  An interactive Covector Fluids solver on a MAC grid whose vortex structure is
  extracted live as discrete vortex filaments (Weissmann–Pinkall), built around
  covMG-LOBPCG: a gauge-covariant geometric multigrid eigensolver for the
  smallest eigenpair of the U(1) connection Laplacian, with a parallel-transport
  (covariant subdivision) prolongation, its exact adjoint as restriction, and an
  A-energy-optimal coarse-correction step. The hierarchy is built in one O(N)
  pass from the operator's own edge data, gauge-equivariance holds by
  construction, and the outer iteration count does not grow under refinement, so
  the solver pulls ahead of zero-setup polynomial acceleration under refinement
  on abelian and non-abelian operator families and on the wake operators
  themselves. Includes an SU(N) generalization and a Wilson-action Monte Carlo
  harness.
preferred-citation:
